# Environment files — never commit these. Today .env holds only the Supabase
# URL and the publishable (anon) key, which are safe to expose, but a tracked
# .env is how a SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY ends up in git history. Keep an
# .env.example with placeholder values instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
